Found the answer.  Both replies were partially correct but there was an
additional problem:  the backticks were OK but the inside single quotes in
the command string, while OK in a terminal, were messing it up in the
crontab even after adding the backslashes.  The correct crontab command
for tcsh and bash is:
            touch home.total.`/usr/bin/date +\%m_\%d_\%y`.pax

S. Stoddard

