Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: Compaq Computer Corporation
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.os.vms,comp.unix.osf.osf1

-tune host is the equivalent of /optimize=tune=host
-arch host is the equivalent of /architecture=host

arch controls  is the lowest processor model the code must run on,
while the tuning center is at least as late model that should be used
as the "sweet spot" for scheduling, etc.  e.g. -arch ev56 -tune ev6
allows byte/word instructions, which are present on ev56 and later,
but tunes preferentially for ev6.

Kent Glossop, GEM Compiler System, Compaq





