> Before you buy.

I had a problem once with default tcp buffer sizes & X11.  Remoted
Xdisplays crawled - run "x11perf -repeat 2 -putimage100" (or something
like that) from a remote machine.  If it's dead slow compared to 
running on a local display (:0) try using dxkerneltuner to change
the inet tcpsendspace and tcprcvspace from 32768 to 4096. Reboot and
check speed again.

Another thing I would try is running Dec/Compaq's utility "sys_check".
It's a utilty their field offices distribute (might be on their web
site?).  Generates a .html report of the system configuration (over
500 pages ...).  It also generates some system tuning suggestions
(kernel parameter mods) based on your configuration.
If nothing else, the output can be shipped to Compaq for analysis
by their engineers.

Hope this helps,
-Bob Arendt



