In article <ruls9vqslg787@corp.supernews.com>, "Chakrapani" <kcpani@reliable-net.net> writes:
> I installed DIA(the DEC Event utility) and while installing it says that I
> need to get some license?  Does anyone know what that license is for?

There are 2 parts to DECevent, and only one requires a license.

The free part is the translation and reporting part. This allows you to see
what errors are being logged. No license is required for this functionality.

The license only part is the intelligence that analyzes errors and does the
fancy stuff. This license is usually available only as part of a DECpaq
maintenance contract.

