On Sun, 26 Sep 1999, Steve Stoddard wrote:

> I want to use a crontab command to write daily archives to files having
> the dates embedded in the filenames.  A FAQ showed me how create such
> files at the command prompt, as for example, 'touch home.total.`date
> '+%m_%d_%y'`.pax' creates the file 'home.total.09_26_99.pax'.  I cannot
> get this same command to work in a crontab.  The crontab itself is OK,
> because 'touch filename' works.  What am I doing wrong?  I'm running
> Tru64 UNIX 4.0E.  Thanks!

I'm almost certain the problem comes from the fact that 'date' can't be
found due to its directory missing from the PATH environment variable
when running from cron. (Cron doesn't execute any of /etc/profile or
$HOME/.profile before running your command).

Specify the full path to 'date' instead and you should be all set.


-- 

