I think you've asked the wrong question.
The message in the logfile just tells you that
your proc subsystem isn't configured for your machines
need.  /sbin/sysconfig -q proc should contain a thread-max
value of 2048.
take a look at the Tuning Guide in the documentation it
tells you how to change the value. dxkerneltuner will also
assist you by doing this. Depending on the tasks teh machine
is performing, it's quite likely that some vm parameters also
have to be adjusted.
The question who is consuming the kernelthreads. I guess
the buest thing to obtain an overview is a little script
with ps -m -Opsr -p<PID>


If you want a monitoring tool for your threaded program,
man vti  (if you're running V4.0F) if you're using V4.0D
or E,  there was a recent announcement about the kit
available on the network.

Pit



