In article <37E8F7F8.D77A5A12@email.uc.edu>,
Arum Han  <hana@email.uc.edu> wrote:
> Probably just add that file in /sbin/init.d and link that file
> from /sbin/rc3.d? Please advice me.

You got it. Note that the files in /sbin/init.d may get called with the
argument "start", "stop", "restart", or "reload" (at least). If you're
using a recent Apache you can probably just have it call "apachectl $1",
since apachectl takes the right arguments already... in fact you could
just symlink init.d/apache to /usr/local/apache/sbin/apachectl.

