My experience with "ltf" was on DECs Ultrix systems (MIPS platform).
I think it is a "better-than-nothing" tool to import ANSI tapes to 
an Ultrix/OSF1 system. The biggest drawback probably is the lack
of multivolume support. Maybe you will also encounter some weird VMS
record organization not supported by ltf (dunno, I'm no DEC expert).
If I remember correctly there also was trouble with the tape device drivers,
but this might have changed with OSF1.
The other direction (UNIX -> ANSI tape) will give you more trouble,
because an ordinary UNIX has no concept of "records" as opposed to proprietary
OSes like VMS or IBMs MVS. 
At our site we had developed an own tool to handle that.

If my memory serves me correctly IBM once offered a tool "NetTape" (or so)
running on their AIX but possibly also on other UNIces. Dunno if it's still
offered, check out their web-page (http://www.ibm.com) 



