A couple of notes have been posted asking how to obtain some of the most
recent ports of the setiathome application for Alpha processors running
Tru64 UNIX, OpenVMS, NT, and Linux.  Ports for the first two of these
have been done and uploaded to the SETI folks at roughly the same time
we made them available internally at Compaq.  However for reasons we do
not understand, the SETI folks have not placed the new Tru64 UNIX
version
on their download site.  Please note that, contrary to some speculation
I've seen posted, the reasons are NOT because of any desire by anyone at
Compaq to withhold these from the general public.  We would like nothing
better than to see these made widely available, but those of us here
involved with doing these ports believe it would be a violation of
the understanding under which this software was provided to us to bypass
the SETI distribution mechanism.

The engineer doing the new Alpha NT port has just completed and uploaded
that image.  In addition, a higher-performance OpenVMS port is in the
works.  Regarding the Alpha Linux version, we are working on providing
a fast port but it may need to wait for a couple tools currently under
development to mature a little to make this effort worthwhile.

We hope that the SETI folks will make the Tru64 UNIX port (and the
upcoming ports) available soon.

--
David A. Long
Compaq Computer Corporation



