In article <7r383q$mi4$1@fddinewz.oit.unc.edu>,
	frey@dove.bme.unc.edu (Eric Frey) writes:
> Just recently we have started getting the following messages on our
> Alphaserver 1000:
> tu0: transmit FIFO underflow: threshold raised to: 512 bytes
> tu0: link up: negotiated 100BaseTX: half duplex
> 
> These start at raised to 256, then 512, then 1024, then store and forward.
> I'm not sure if it is related, but the nfs service sometimes gets locked up.
> When this happens I get the following message on the console and in
> /var/adm/messages:
> malloc_mem_alloc: no space in map

I'm not exactly sure about the "no space in map" messages, but the FIFO
messages can create a slight problem because you've got your NIC set to
auto-negotiate.  It seems that the NIC (a DE500 I assume) will renegotiate 
it's speed when it gets the FIFO underflow which will actually drop your
connection for a short time.  Although this shouldn't stop your nfs service
it probably doesn't help.  We had a similar probably with a couple of 8400s 
here and ended up disabling autonegotiate on the card and the switch which
fix the problem.

Andrew
