I believe that, by default, UFS file systems on the DEC Alpha reserve
10% of their space. You can see this with a "dumpfs /dev/rrz3c" command.
Look for "minfree" near the top of the page. This will probably read
10%. Use the tunefs command to change this value. I typically use 1% on
disks bigger than 9GB.  From past comments from Compaq/DEC people, this
value is probably reasonable for a multi-GB modern disk.

Richard Eckman
