of our programs. Build the l.ibrary was not a real problem. But the use
of the malloc debug library was a real one. Even with the following
simple test program the malloc debug library showed an error regarding
freeing an none-allocated memory region.

void main()
{ char *a=(char*)malloc(10);
    free(a);
    exit(0);
}

The error occure in exit(). When we use _exit() every thing is fine. The
same happens within getopt(). My guess is that because of the dynamic
linkage some libc functions are bound to the regulare malloc/free
functions and other to the malloc debug libary. We tried to use static
linakge with -no_shared but it didnt helped.

Does one of you know how to get it work?

