In article <37C6CD5F.AC01F0AA@glue.umd.edu>, Vinesh Gupta <vinesh@glue.umd.edu> writes:

>Hi,
>We have two Digital machines that are giving these errors. We upgraded
>the latest firmware
>and the OS to 4.0.d, still the memory errors are there:
>
>Aug  2 14:29:32 kilimanjaro vmunix: trap: invalid memory read access
>from kernel mode

[ Some details deleted ]

>Aug  2 14:29:32 kilimanjaro vmunix: panic (cpu 0): kernel memory fault

These aren't memory errors.  These are kernel software errors that are
cause by drivers or other kernel components that are trying to access
memory that isn't there; a bug.  One cause that I'm familiar with is
using an older version of the CLC Media Changer Driver on a newer
version system.  If you're using the CLC drivers, use the one that
came on the Associated Products CDROM.


--
Alan Rollow				alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com




