Print filters provide the device specific commands for
printing features such as duplex and landscape printing.
Lpd remote printing, printcaps with rp and rm values set, do
not use print filters so duplex and landscape printing
features are not available.

A tcp/ip printing environment, mentioned in my previous
note, does use print filters so printing options are
available. What is available is dependent on the print filter
in use.

If the system doesn't include a configuration for your
printer you can try the following configurations.

For PostScript printers:

        ln03r, ps_level1, ps_level2

        These printer setups convert text files to PostScript and
        provide duplex, and landscape printing.

For a PCL printer try the ln17 printer setup which also
provides duplex and landscape printing. You can also create
a printer configuration file for use with the pcfof print
and include other hardware features such as input and outut
paper tray selection. Look at the file /usr/lbin/pcf/template.pcf.

-----------------

Kevin Oberman wrote:

> meikled@my-deja.com writes:
>
> > In article <01bef29a$e32216a0$761a51d8@default>,
> >   "darcul" <darcul@escape.ca> wrote:
