> > the Jetprint/Jetdirect software is available for
> > Tru64 4.0F?  I remember using it a few years ago,
> > but I've been out of touch with Digital Unix for
> > a while now, and can't find it.  I seem to
> > remember it being included in the software
> > library distribution, but it seems to have gone
> > from there.  No sign at hp.com or compaq.com,
> > either.
>
> Printing to a JetDirect requires no special software, although added
> functionality does.
>
> Simply create printcap entries for the printer with one entry
> specifying "rp=text" and the other specifying "rp=raw". Use the first
> entry to print plain test files and the other for PostScript, HPGL,
> and bitmaps. ("text" converts <LF> to <LF><CR>)
>
> A better choice is to get LPRng from:
> http://www.astart.com/lprng/LPRng.html
> and the HP filter software from:
> ftp://ftp.astart.com/pub/LPRng/ifhp-current.tgz
>
> These will allow the specification of things like duplex, landscape,
> and the like. They completely replace the various commands and
> daemons that come with DU, and they work beautifully, once you get the
> configuration right. They also allow you to use only a single 'raw'
> queue for all output.
> --
> R. Kevin Oberman, Network Engineer
> Energy Sciences Network (ESnet)
> Ernest Orlando Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory (Berkeley Lab)
> E-mail: oberman@es.net                          Phone: +1 510 486-8634

